{title: Glory to His Name (Down at the Cross)}
{artist: Elisha A. Hoffman / John H. Stockton}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Worship in Song (Kansas City, Missouri: Lillenas Publishing, 1972), # 81)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Down at the cross where my [C]Savior [G]died,
[G]Down where for cleansing from sin I [D]cried,
[G]There to my heart was the [C]blood ap[G]plied;
[G]Glory [D7]to His [G]name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Glory to His [G]name, glory to His [D]name:
[G]There to my heart was the [C]blood ap[G]plied;
[G]Glory [D7]to His [G]name!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I am so wondrously [C]saved from [G]sin,
[G]Jesus so sweetly abides with[D]in;
[G]There at the cross where He [C]took me [G]in;
[G]Glory [D7]to His [G]name!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Oh, precious fountain that [C]saves from [G]sin,
[G]I am so glad I have entered [D]in;
[G]There Jesus saves me and [C]keeps me [G]clean;
[G]Glory [D7]to His [G]name!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Come to this fountain so [C]rich and [G]sweet,
[G]Cast thy poor soul at the Savior’s [D]feet;
[G]Plunge in today, and be [C]made com[G]plete;
[G]Glory [D7]to His [G]name!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
